addEdge -- A method for adding edges to a graph
***********************************************

  * Usage: 
        H = addEdges' (G, L)
        H = addEdge (G, S)
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, This List should be composed of
        other Lists, just as one would input an edge set
      * S, a *note set: (Macaulay2Doc)Set,, This is used when only one edge
        needs to be used via addEdge
  * Outputs:
      * H, a *note graph: Graph,, The Graph with the new edge

Description
===========

This method will take in a Graph and a List of new edges, and output a graph
with these new edges along with the previous edges.

+------------------------------------+
|i1 : H = cycleGraph 4;              |
+------------------------------------+
|i2 : G = addEdge(H, set {0,2})      |
|                                    |
|o2 = Graph{0 => {1, 2, 3}}          |
|           1 => {0, 2}              |
|           2 => {0, 1, 3}           |
|           3 => {0, 2}              |
|                                    |
|o2 : Graph                          |
+------------------------------------+
|i3 : G = addEdges'(H, {{0,2},{3,1}})|
|                                    |
|o3 = Graph{0 => {1, 2, 3}}          |
|           1 => {0, 2, 3}           |
|           2 => {0, 1, 3}           |
|           3 => {0, 1, 2}           |
|                                    |
|o3 : Graph                          |
+------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note addVertices: addVertex, -- A method for adding a set of vertices to a
    graph

