barbellGraph -- Returns the barbell graph
*****************************************

  * Usage: 
        G = barbellGraph n
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
  * Outputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, The barbell graph

Description
===========

The barbell graph corresponding to an integer n is formed by the disjoint union
of two complete graphs on n vertices joined together by exactly on edge
connecting these complete graphs.

+-------------------------------------+
|i1 : G = barbellGraph 6              |
|                                     |
|o1 = Graph{0 => {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}     }|
|           1 => {0, 2, 3, 4, 5}      |
|           2 => {0, 1, 3, 4, 5}      |
|           3 => {0, 1, 2, 4, 5}      |
|           4 => {0, 1, 2, 3, 5}      |
|           5 => {0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 6}   |
|           6 => {5, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11} |
|           7 => {6, 8, 9, 10, 11}    |
|           8 => {6, 7, 9, 10, 11}    |
|           9 => {6, 7, 8, 10, 11}    |
|           10 => {6, 7, 8, 9, 11}    |
|           11 => {6, 7, 8, 9, 10}    |
|                                     |
|o1 : Graph                           |
+-------------------------------------+

