barycenter -- Returns the barycenter of a grah
**********************************************

  * Usage: 
        H = barycenter G
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * H, a *note graph: Graph,, The barycenter of G

Description
===========

The barycenter of a graph is the subgraph induced by all the vertices with
eccentricity equal to the graph's radius, in other words, it is the subgraph
induced by the center of a graph.

+--------------------------------+
|i1 : barycenter pathGraph 6     |
|                                |
|o1 = Graph{2 => {3}}            |
|           3 => {2}             |
|                                |
|o1 : Graph                      |
+--------------------------------+
|i2 : barycenter completeGraph 6 |
|                                |
|o2 = Graph{0 => {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}}|
|           1 => {0, 2, 3, 4, 5} |
|           2 => {0, 1, 3, 4, 5} |
|           3 => {0, 1, 2, 4, 5} |
|           4 => {0, 1, 2, 3, 5} |
|           5 => {0, 1, 2, 3, 4} |
|                                |
|o2 : Graph                      |
+--------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note center: center, -- Returns the center of a graph

Ways to use barycenter:
=======================

