center -- Returns the center of a graph
***************************************

  * Usage: 
        L = center G
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, This is a list of the vertices of
        G that form the center of G

Description
===========

The center of a graph G is defined to be the set of all vertices of G such that
the eccentricity of the vertex is equal to the graph's radius. This list often
will contain 1 member, for example, path graphs on with an odd amount of
vertices.  It can also contain all the vertices (such as complete graphs).

+-------------------------------+
|i1 : center graphLibrary "dart"|
|                               |
|o1 = {2}                       |
|                               |
|o1 : List                      |
+-------------------------------+

