children -- returns the children of a vertex of a digraph
*********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        C = children (D, v)
  * Inputs:
      * D, a *note digraph: Digraph,, 
      * v, a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, the vertex that we want to find
        the children of
  * Outputs:
      * C, a *note set: (Macaulay2Doc)Set,, a set of the children of v

Description
===========

The children of v are the all the vertices u such that {v,u} is in the edge set
of the digraph D. So the children of a vertex v are exactly those vertices on a
directed graph that v points to.

+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : D = digraph({a,b,c,d,e},{{a,b},{b,c},{b,d},{e,b}});|
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : children(D, b)                                     |
|                                                        |
|o2 = set {c, d}                                         |
|                                                        |
|o2 : Set                                                |
+--------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

