circularLadder -- Returns a circular ladder graph
*************************************************

  * Usage: 
        G = circularLadder n
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
  * Outputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, The circular ladder graph

Description
===========

The circular ladder graph corresponding to an integer n is a ladder of size n
with two extra edges that connect the each top vertex with its respective
bottom vertex. This creates two cycles, one inside and the other outside, that
are connected by edges.

+--------------------------+
|i1 : G = circularLadder 5 |
|                          |
|o1 = Graph{0 => {1, 4, 5}}|
|           1 => {0, 2, 6} |
|           2 => {1, 3, 7} |
|           3 => {2, 4, 8} |
|           4 => {0, 3, 9} |
|           5 => {0, 6, 9} |
|           6 => {1, 5, 7} |
|           7 => {2, 6, 8} |
|           8 => {3, 7, 9} |
|           9 => {4, 5, 8} |
|                          |
|o1 : Graph                |
+--------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note ladderGraph: ladderGraph, -- Returns a ladder graph

