clusteringCoefficient -- a method for computing the clustering coefficient of a Graph
*************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        c = clusteringCoefficient(G, v)
        g = clusteringCoefficient(G)
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 
      * v, a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, v should be a member of the
        vertex set of G
  * Outputs:
      * c, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, The local clustering
        coefficient for G relative to v.
      * g, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, The global clustering
        coefficient for G.

Description
===========

The clustering coefficient is a measure of the degree to which nodes in a graph
tend to cluster together. The global clustering coefficient gives an overall
indication of the interconnectedness of the graph. The local clustering
coefficient gives an indication of how embedded a single vertex is in the
graph.

+------------------------------------------+
|i1 : clusteringCoefficient cycleGraph 4   |
|                                          |
|o1 = 0                                    |
|                                          |
|o1 : QQ                                   |
+------------------------------------------+
|i2 : clusteringCoefficient completeGraph 4|
|                                          |
|o2 = 1                                    |
|                                          |
|o2 : QQ                                   |
+------------------------------------------+

