complementGraph -- Returns the complement of a graph
****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        G' = complementGraph G
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * G', a *note graph: Graph,, The complement graph of G

Description
===========

The complement graph of a graph G is the graph G^c where any two vertices are
adjacent in G^c iff they are not adjacent in G. The original vertex set is
preserved, only the edges are changed.

+-----------------------+
|i1 : G = cycleGraph 4  |
|                       |
|o1 = Graph{0 => {1, 3}}|
|           1 => {0, 2} |
|           2 => {1, 3} |
|           3 => {0, 2} |
|                       |
|o1 : Graph             |
+-----------------------+
|i2 : complementGraph G |
|                       |
|o2 = Graph{0 => {2}}   |
|           1 => {3}    |
|           2 => {0}    |
|           3 => {1}    |
|                       |
|o2 : Graph             |
+-----------------------+

Ways to use complementGraph:
============================

  * "complementGraph(Graph)"

