degeneracy -- Computes the degeneracy of a graph
************************************************

  * Usage: 
        d = degeneracy G
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 

Description
===========

The degeneracy of a graph is the maximum degree of all vertices in any subgraph
of G.  This is essentially equivalent to the coloring number of G, which is the
least number k such that there exists an ordering of the vertices of G in which
each vertex has less than k neighbors earlier in the ordering.  The coloring
number is equal to the degeneracy plus one.

+--------------------------+
|i1 : G = completeGraph 10;|
+--------------------------+
|i2 : degeneracy G         |
|                          |
|o2 = 9                    |
+--------------------------+

Ways to use degeneracy:
=======================

  * "degeneracy(Graph)"

