degree(Digraph,Thing) -- returns the degree of a vertex in a digraph
********************************************************************

  * Function: *note degree: (Macaulay2Doc)degree,
  * Usage: 
        x = degree(D,v)
  * Inputs:
      * D, a *note digraph: Digraph,, 
      * v, a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, a vertex in the graph/digraph
  * Outputs:
      * x, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 

Description
===========

In a simple graph, the degree of a vertex is the number of neighbors of the
vertex. In a digraph, we define the degree of a vertex to be the number of
elements in the unique union of the parents and children of the vertex.

+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : D = digraph({1,2,3,4},{{1,2},{2,3},{3,4},{4,2},{2,4}});|
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : degree(D, 3)                                           |
|                                                            |
|o2 = 2                                                      |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : degree(D, 2)                                           |
|                                                            |
|o3 = 3                                                      |
+------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note neighbors: neighbors, -- returns the neighbors of a vertex in a graph
  * *note parents: parents, -- returns the parents of a vertex on a digraph
  * *note children: children, -- returns the children of a vertex of a digraph

