===========

In a directed graph, we define the degree into a vertex or the "in-degree" of a
vertex to be the number of parents of that vertex. Intuitively, this give the
number of edges that point into the vertex.

+------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : D = digraph({1,2,3,4},{{1,2},{2,3},{3,4},{4,2}});|
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : degreeIn(D, 2)                                   |
|                                                      |
|o2 = 2                                                |
+------------------------------------------------------+

