degreeMatrix -- Returns the degree matrix of a graph
****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        D = degreeMatrix G
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * D, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, The degree matrix of graph G

Description
===========

The degree matrix is the n by n diagonal matrix (where n is the number of
vertices in the vertex set of the graph G) indexed by the vertices of G where
A_(u,u) is the degree of vertex u. The degree of a vertex u is the number of
edges such that {u,v} is an edge for any v also in the vertex set. This matrix
is always diagonal.

+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : G = graph({1,2,3,4,5},{{1,2},{2,3},{3,4},{3,5},{4,5}});|
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : degreeMatrix G                                         |
|                                                            |
|o2 = | 1 0 0 0 0 |                                          |
|     | 0 2 0 0 0 |                                          |
|     | 0 0 3 0 0 |                                          |
|     | 0 0 0 2 0 |                                          |
|     | 0 0 0 0 2 |                                          |
|                                                            |
|              5       5                                     |
|o2 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                      |
+------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note adjacencyMatrix: adjacencyMatrix, -- Returns the adjacency matrix of
    a Graph or Digraph
  * *note laplacianMatrix: laplacianMatrix, -- Returns the laplacian matrix of
    a graph
  * *note degree: (Macaulay2Doc)degree,

Ways to use degreeMatrix:
=========================

  * "degreeMatrix(Digraph)"

