degreeOut -- returns the "out-degree" of a vertex in a digraph
**************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        x = degreeIn (D, v)
  * Inputs:
      * D, a *note digraph: Digraph,, 
      * v, a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, a vertex of D
  * Outputs:
      * x, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 

Description
===========

In a directed graph, we define the degree out of a vertex or the "out-degree"
of a vertex to be the number of children of that vertex. Intuitively, this give
the number of edges pointing out of a vertex to another vertex.

+------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : D = digraph({1,2,3,4},{{1,2},{2,3},{3,4},{4,2}});|
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : degreeOut(D, 2)                                  |
|                                                      |
|o2 = 1                                                |
+------------------------------------------------------+

