density -- computes the density of a graph
******************************************

  * Usage: 
        d = density G
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * d, a *note rational number: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,, the density of G

Description
===========

A dense graph has a high edge to vertex ratio, whereas a sparse graph has a low
edge to vertex ratio.  Density is equal to 2*|E| divided by |V|*(|V|-1).  A
complete graph has density 1; the minimal density of any graph is 0.

+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : G = graph({{1,2},{2,3},{3,4},{4,2},{1,4}},EntryMode=>"edges");|
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : density G                                                     |
|                                                                   |
|     5                                                             |
|o2 = -                                                             |
|     6                                                             |
|                                                                   |
|o2 : QQ                                                            |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

