diameter(Graph) -- Computes the diameter of a graph
***************************************************

  * Function: *note diameter: (Macaulay2Doc)diameter,
  * Usage: 
        d = diameter G
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, The diameter of G

Description
===========

The diameter of a graph is the maximum of the distances between all the
vertexSet of G.  If the graph is not connected, the diameter is infinity.

+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : G = graph({{1,2},{2,3},{3,4}},EntryMode=>"edges");|
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : d = diameter G                                    |
|                                                       |
|o2 = 3                                                 |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : G = graph({1,2,3,4},{{2,3},{3,4}});               |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : d = diameter G                                    |
|                                                       |
|o4 = infinity                                          |
|                                                       |
|o4 : InfiniteNumber                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note distance: distance, -- Computes the distance between two vertexSet in
    a graph
  * *note distanceMatrix: distanceMatrix, -- Computes the distance matrix of a
    digraph

Ways to use this method:
========================

