digraphTranspose -- returns the transpose of a Digraph
******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        G = digraphTranspose D
  * Inputs:
      * D, a *note digraph: Digraph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * G, a *note digraph: Digraph,, the transpose digraph of D

Description
===========

The transpose of a digraph D is the graph formed by taking every edge (u,v) in
D and changing it to (v,u). Intuitively, it reverses the direction of all the
edges while keeping the same vertex set.  One can also view the transpose in
terms of adjacency matrices, where the adjacency matrix of the transpose of D
is the transpose of the adjacency matrix of D. In this way, we quickly see that
the transpose of a transpose digraph is the original digraph, and that this
operator is trivial for simple graphs since they have symmetric matrices.

+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : D = digraph ({{1,2},{2,3},{3,4},{4,1},{1,3},{4,2}},EntryMode=>"edges")|
|                                                                           |
|o1 = Digraph{1 => {2, 3}}                                                  |
|             2 => {3}                                                      |
|             3 => {4}                                                      |
|             4 => {1, 2}                                                   |
|                                                                           |
|o1 : Digraph                                                               |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : D' = digraphTranspose D                                               |
|                                                                           |
|o2 = Digraph{1 => {4}   }                                                  |
|             2 => {1, 4}                                                   |
|             3 => {1, 2}                                                   |
|             4 => {3}                                                      |
|                                                                           |
|o2 : Digraph                                                               |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : D'' = digraphTranspose D'                                             |
|                                                                           |
|o3 = Digraph{1 => {2, 3}}                                                  |
|             2 => {3}                                                      |
|             3 => {4}                                                      |
|             4 => {1, 2}                                                   |
|                                                                           |
|o3 : Digraph                                                               |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use digraphTranspose:
=============================

  * "digraphTranspose(Digraph)"

