distance -- Computes the distance between two vertexSet in a graph
******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        d = distance(G,v,u)
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 
      * v, a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, 
      * u, a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, 
  * Outputs:
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, The distance between vertexSet
        v and u

Description
===========

The distance between two vertexSet is calculated as the number of edges in the
shortest path between the two vertexSet.  If the two vertexSet are not
connected, the distance between them is infinity by convention.

+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : G = graph({{1,2},{2,3},{3,4}},EntryMode=>"edges");|
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : d = distance (G,1,4)                              |
|                                                       |
|o2 = 3                                                 |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : G = graph({1,2,3,4},{{2,3},{3,4}});               |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : d = distance(G, 1, 4)                             |
|                                                       |
|o4 = infinity                                          |
|                                                       |
|o4 : InfiniteNumber                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note diameter(Graph): diameter_lpGraph_rp, -- Computes the diameter of a
    graph
