edgeConnectivity -- computes the edge connectivity of a graph
*************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        C = edgeConnectivity G
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * C, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the edge connectivity of a
        graph

Description
===========

The edge connectivity of a graph is the smallest amount of edges that need be
removed from a graph to make it not connected.  This corresponds to the size of
the edge cuts.  A not connected graph has edge connectivity equal to 0.

