edges -- Returns the edges of a digraph or graph
************************************************

  * Usage: 
        E = edges D
        E = edges G
  * Inputs:
      * D, a *note digraph: Digraph,, 
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * E, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, The edges of digraph D or graph G

Description
===========

The edges of a graph are pairs (or ordered pairs if we are dealing with
digraphs) of vertices that are connected in a graph. Any edge must be a member
of the collection of subsets of the vertex set of a graph.

+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : D = digraph({{1,2},{2,1},{3,1}},EntryMode=>"edges");|
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : edges D                                             |
|                                                         |
|o2 = {{1, 2}, {2, 1}, {3, 1}}                            |
|                                                         |
|o2 : List                                                |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : G = cycleGraph 4;                                   |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
