expansion -- returns the expansion of a graph
*********************************************

  * Usage: 
        h=expansion G
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * h, a *note rational number: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,, the expansion of a graph
        G

Description
===========

The expansion of a subset S of vertices is the ratio of the number of edges
leaving S and the size of S. The (edge) expansion of a graph G is the minimal
expansion of all not too large subsets of the vertex set. The expansion of a
disconnected graph is 0 whereas the expansion of the complete graph on n
vertices is ceiling(n/2)

+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : G = graph({{1, 2}, {1, 3}, {2, 3}, {3, 4}},EntryMode=>"edges");|
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : expansion G                                                    |
|                                                                    |
|o2 = 1                                                              |
|                                                                    |
|o2 : QQ                                                             |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : expansion pathGraph 7                                          |
|                                                                    |
|     1                                                              |
|o3 = -                                                              |
|     3                                                              |
|                                                                    |
|o3 : QQ                                                             |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use expansion:
======================

  * "expansion(Graph)"

