friendshipGraph -- Returns a friendship Graph
*********************************************

  * Usage: 
        G = friendshipGraph n
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
  * Outputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 

Description
===========

Friendship graphs of size n are a special case of windmill graphs. A friendship
graph of size n is n 3-cycles that all share one common vertex.

+-----------------------------------------+
|i1 : G = friendshipGraph 4               |
|                                         |
|o1 = Graph{0 => {1, 3, 5, 7, 2, 4, 6, 8}}|
|           1 => {0, 2}                   |
|           2 => {0, 1}                   |
|           3 => {0, 4}                   |
|           4 => {0, 3}                   |
|           5 => {0, 6}                   |
|           6 => {0, 5}                   |
|           7 => {0, 8}                   |
|           8 => {0, 7}                   |
|                                         |
|o1 : Graph                               |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i2 : H = windmillGraph (3,4)             |
|                                         |
|o2 = Graph{0 => {1, 3, 5, 7, 2, 4, 6, 8}}|
|           1 => {0, 2}                   |
|           2 => {0, 1}                   |
|           3 => {0, 4}                   |
|           4 => {0, 3}                   |
|           5 => {0, 6}                   |
|           6 => {0, 5}                   |
|           7 => {0, 8}                   |
|           8 => {0, 7}                   |
|                                         |
|o2 : Graph                               |
+-----------------------------------------+

