girth -- A method for computing the girth of a graph
****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        g = girth G
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * g, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the girth of G

Description
===========

This method computes the girth (the smallest n such that G contains an n-cycle)
of any graph. If the graph has no n-cycle as a subgraph, the output will be
infinity.

+--------------------------+
|i1 : girth completeGraph 6|
|                          |
|o1 = 3                    |
+--------------------------+
|i2 : girth pathGraph 6    |
|                          |
|o2 = infinity             |
|                          |
|o2 : InfiniteNumber       |
+--------------------------+

Ways to use girth:
==================

  * "girth(Graph)"

