graphPower -- constructs a graph raised to a power
**************************************************

  * Usage: 
        G' = graphPower(G,k)
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 
      * k, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
  * Outputs:
      * G', a *note graph: Graph,, graph G to the kth power

Description
===========

G^k is the graph with the same vertices as G, where the vertices of G^k are
adjacent if they are separated by distance less than or equal to k in graph G.
If the diameter of G is d, G^d is the complete graph with the same number of
vertices as G.

+-----------------------------+
|i1 : G = cycleGraph 6;       |
+-----------------------------+
|i2 : graphPower(G,2)         |
|                             |
|o2 = Graph{0 => {1, 2, 4, 5}}|
|           1 => {0, 2, 3, 5} |
|           2 => {0, 1, 3, 4} |
|           3 => {1, 2, 4, 5} |
|           4 => {0, 2, 3, 5} |
|           5 => {0, 1, 3, 4} |
|                             |
|o2 : Graph                   |
+-----------------------------+

See also
========

