hasEulerianTrail -- determines whether a graph or a digraph has an Eulerian trail
*********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        E = hasEulerianTrail G
        E = hasEulerianTrail D
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 
      * D, a *note digraph: Digraph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * E, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, whether G or D has an
        Eulerian trail

Description
===========

A graph has an Eulerian trail if there is a path in the graph that visits each
edge exactly once.  A digraph has a Eulerian trail if there is a directed path
in the graph that visits each edge exactly once.  An Eulerian trail is also
called an Eulerian path.  Unconnected graphs can have a Eulerian trail, but all
vertices of degree greater than 0 of a graph (or all vertices of degree greater
than 0 in the underlying graph of a digraph) must belong to a single connected
component.

+----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : G = cycleGraph 5;                              |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : hasEulerianTrail G                             |
|                                                    |
|o2 = true                                           |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : D = digraph(toList(1..4), {{1,2},{2,3},{3,4}});|
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : hasEulerianTrail D                             |
|                                                    |
|o4 = true                                           |
+----------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note isEulerian: isEulerian, -- determines if a graph or digraph is
    Eulerian

