isReachable -- checks if a vertex u is reachable from a vertex v
****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        r = isReachable(D, u, v)
  * Inputs:
      * D, a *note digraph: Digraph,, 
      * u, a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, this is the vertex that we are
        attempting to reach
      * v, a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, this is the vertex that we are
        starting from
  * Outputs:
      * r, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, whether or not us is
        reachable from v

Description
===========

In a Digraph D, a vertex u of D is reachable from another vertex v of D if u is
a descendant of v. Alternatively, u is reachable from v if there is some set of
vertices u_0, ... , u_n such that u_n = u and u_0 = v and (u_i, u_i+1) is and
edge of D for all i from 0 to n-1.

+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : D = digraph({a,b,c,d,e},{{a,b},{b,c},{b,d},{e,b}});|
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : isReachable(D, e, a)                               |
|                                                        |
|o2 = false                                              |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : isReachable(D, d, e)                               |
|                                                        |
|o3 = true                                               |
+--------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

