isRigid -- checks if a graph is rigid
*************************************

  * Usage: 
        r = isRigid G
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * r, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

A drawing of a graph is rigid in the plane if any continuous motion of the
vertices that preserve edge lengths must preserve the distance between every
pair of vertices.  A graph is generically rigid if any drawing of the graph
with vertices in general position is rigid. This method uses Laman's Theorem to
determine if a graph is rigid or not.

+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : G = cycleGraph 4;                |
+--------------------------------------+
|i2 : isRigid G                        |
|                                      |
|o2 = false                            |
+--------------------------------------+
|i3 : G' = addEdges' (G, {{1,1},{3,1}})|
|                                      |
|o3 = Graph{0 => {1, 3}      }         |
