isSimple -- checks if a graph is simple
***************************************

  * Usage: 
        r = isSimple G
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * r, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

A graph is said to be simple if it has a maximum of one edge between each
vertex, contains no loops (vertices connected to themselves by edges), and is
undirected. Since the Graph Type does not allow for multiple edges and directed
edges, it is sufficient to check that the graph has no loops.

+---------------------------------+
|i1 : G = cycleGraph 5;           |
+---------------------------------+
|i2 : isSimple G                  |
|                                 |
|o2 = true                        |
+---------------------------------+
|i3 : G' = addEdge (G, set {1,1});|
+---------------------------------+
|i4 : isSimple G'                 |
|                                 |
|o4 = false                       |
+---------------------------------+

Ways to use isSimple:
=====================

  * "isSimple(Graph)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note isSimple: isSimple, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

