isStronglyConnected -- checks if a digraph is strongly connected
****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        r = isStronglyConnected D
  * Inputs:
      * D, a *note digraph: Digraph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * r, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

A digraph is said to be strongly connected if for each vertex u of D, any other
vertex of D is reachable from u. An equivalent definition is that D is strongly
connected if the distance matrix of D has only positive terms in the
non-diagonal entries.

+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : D = digraph({1,2,3,4},{{1,2},{2,3},{3,4},{4,2}});       |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : isStronglyConnected D                                   |
|                                                             |
|o2 = false                                                   |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : D' = digraph({1,2,3,4},{{1,2},{2,1},{2,3},{3,4},{4,2}});|
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isStronglyConnected D'                                  |
|                                                             |
|o4 = true                                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note isWeaklyConnected: isWeaklyConnected, -- checks if a digraph is
    weakly connected
  * *note distanceMatrix: distanceMatrix, -- Computes the distance matrix of a
    digraph
  * *note isReachable: isReachable, -- checks if a vertex u is reachable from a
    vertex v

