kneserGraph -- constructs a kneser graph of specified size
**********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        G = kneserGraph(n,k)
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * k, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
  * Outputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, The kneser graph constructed with vertices
        corresponding to the k-element subsets of a set of n elements.

Description
===========

A kneser graph (n,k) has vertices corresponding to the k-element subsets of a
set of n elements, where two vertices are adjacent if and only if their
corresponding k-element subsets are disjoint.

+--------------------------+
|i1 : G = kneserGraph(5,2) |
|                          |
|o1 = Graph{0 => {5, 8, 9}}|
|           1 => {4, 7, 9} |
|           2 => {3, 6, 9} |
|           3 => {2, 7, 8} |
|           4 => {1, 6, 8} |
|           5 => {0, 6, 7} |
|           6 => {2, 4, 5} |
|           7 => {1, 3, 5} |
|           8 => {0, 3, 4} |
|           9 => {0, 1, 2} |
|                          |
|o1 : Graph                |
+--------------------------+

