laplacianMatrix -- Returns the laplacian matrix of a graph
**********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        L = laplacianMatrix G
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * L, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, the laplacian matrix of graph
        G

Description
===========

The laplacian matrix of a graph is the adjacency matrix of the graph subtracted
from the degree matrix of the graph.

+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : G = graph({1,2,3,4,5},{{1,2},{2,3},{3,4},{3,5},{4,5}});|
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : laplacianMatrix G                                      |
|                                                            |
|o2 = | 1  -1 0  0  0  |                                     |
|     | -1 2  -1 0  0  |                                     |
|     | 0  -1 3  -1 -1 |                                     |
|     | 0  0  -1 2  -1 |                                     |
|     | 0  0  -1 -1 2  |                                     |
|                                                            |
|              5       5                                     |
|o2 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                      |
+------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note adjacencyMatrix: adjacencyMatrix, -- Returns the adjacency matrix of
    a Graph or Digraph
  * *note degreeMatrix: degreeMatrix, -- Returns the degree matrix of a graph

