lollipopGraph -- constructs a lollipop graph
********************************************

  * Usage: 
        G = lollipopGraph (m, n)
  * Inputs:
      * m, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, The number of vertices in the
        complete graph element
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, The length of stem coming out
        of the complete graph element
  * Outputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, The lollipop graph

Description
===========

A lollipop graph is a graph that is the union of two major elements. The
"candy" portion is a complete graph of size m. Coming out of this is the stick
or stem, just a path graph of size n. The combination of these yields a
lollipop graph.

+-----------------------------------+
|i1 : lollipopGraph (6,2)           |
|                                   |
|o1 = Graph{0 => {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}   }|
|           1 => {0, 2, 3, 4, 5}    |
|           2 => {0, 1, 3, 4, 5}    |
|           3 => {0, 1, 2, 4, 5}    |
|           4 => {0, 1, 2, 3, 5}    |
|           5 => {0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 6} |
|           6 => {5, 7}             |
|           7 => {6}                |
|                                   |
|o1 : Graph                         |
+-----------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note rattleGraph: rattleGraph, -- Returns a rattle graph

