radius -- Returns the radius of a graph
***************************************

  * Usage: 
        r = radius G
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * r, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 

Description
===========

The radius of a graph is defined to be the minimum of the eccentricities of the
vertexSet, i.e, the smallest number k such that for some vertex v, the distance
between v and another vertex is less than or equal to k.

+-------------------------------+
|i1 : radius completeGraph 5    |
|                               |
|o1 = 1                         |
+-------------------------------+
|i2 : radius pathGraph 5        |
|                               |
|o2 = 2                         |
+-------------------------------+
|i3 : radius graphLibrary "dart"|
|                               |
|o3 = 1                         |
+-------------------------------+

See also
