spanningForest -- constructs a spanning forest of a graph
*********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        F = spanningForest G
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * F, a *note graph: Graph,, a forest spanning G

Description
===========

A graph is a forest if it is a disjoint collection of trees.  A graph is a tree
if any two vertices are connected by a unique path of edges.  A spanning forest
is a forest that spans all the vectors of G using edges of G.

+-----------------------+
|i1 : G = cycleGraph 5; |
+-----------------------+
|i2 : spanningForest G  |
|                       |
|o2 = Graph{0 => {1, 4}}|
|           1 => {0, 2} |
|           2 => {1, 3} |
|           3 => {2}    |
|           4 => {0}    |
|                       |
|o2 : Graph             |
+-----------------------+

See also
========

  * *note isForest: isForest, -- determines whether a graph is a forest
  * *note isTree: isTree, -- determines whether a graph is a tree

Ways to use spanningForest:
===========================

  * "spanningForest(Graph)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note spanningForest: spanningForest, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

