strongProduct -- a method for taking the strong product of two graphs
*********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        F = strongProduct(G,H)
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 
      * H, a *note graph: Graph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * F, a *note graph: Graph,, The Strong Product of G and H

Description
===========

This method will take in any two graphs and output the strong product of the
two graphs. The vertex set of the strong product of G and H is the cartesian
product of the vertex sets of G and H. The keys for each vertex will be output
as a sequence to represent this clearly. The edge set of the strong product of
G and H is formed by the rule any two distinct vertices (u,u') and (v,v') are
adjacent in G and H if and only if u' is adjacent with v' or u'=v' , and u is
adjacent with v or u = v.

+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : G = graph({1,2},{{1,2}});                                |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : H = graph({3,4,5},{{3,4},{4,5}});                        |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : strongProduct(G,H)                                       |
|                                                              |
|o3 = Graph{{1, 3} => {{2, 3}, {1, 4}, {2, 4}}                }|
|           {1, 4} => {{2, 5}, {1, 3}, {2, 3}, {2, 4}, {1, 5}} |
|           {1, 5} => {{2, 5}, {1, 4}, {2, 4}}                 |
|           {2, 3} => {{1, 3}, {1, 4}, {2, 4}}                 |
|           {2, 4} => {{2, 5}, {1, 3}, {2, 3}, {1, 4}, {1, 5}} |
|           {2, 5} => {{1, 4}, {2, 4}, {1, 5}}                 |
|                                                              |
|o3 : Graph                                                    |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note graphComposition: graphComposition, -- A method for composing two
    graphs
  * *note directProduct: (Macaulay2Doc)directProduct, -- direct product
  * *note cartesianProduct: cartesianProduct, -- Computes the cartesian product
    of two graphs

Ways to use strongProduct:
==========================

  * "strongProduct(Graph,Graph)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note strongProduct: strongProduct, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

