underlyingGraph -- Returns the underlying graph of a digraph
************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        G = underlyingGraph D
  * Inputs:
      * D, a *note digraph: Digraph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, The underlying graph of digraph D

Description
===========

The underlying graph of a digraph is the simple graph constructed by all edges
{u,v} such that (u,v) or (v,u) is a directed edge in the digraph.

+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : D = digraph hashTable{1 => {2,3}, 2 => {1,3}, 3 => {}};|
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : underlyingGraph D                                      |
|                                                            |
|o2 = Graph{1 => {2, 3}}                                     |
|           2 => {1, 3}                                      |
|           3 => {1, 2}                                      |
|                                                            |
|o2 : Graph                                                  |
+------------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use underlyingGraph:
============================

  * "underlyingGraph(Digraph)"

