vertexConnectivity -- computes the vertex connectivity of a graph
*****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        C = vertexConnectivity G
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * C, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the vertex connectivity of a
        graph

Description
===========

The vertex connectivity of a graph is the smallest amount of vertices that need
be removed from a graph to make it not connected or have one vertex.  This
corresponds to the size of the smallest vertex cut.  A not connected graph has
connectivity equal to 0.

+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : G = graph({{1,2},{2,3},{3,1},{3,4},{4,5},{5,3}},EntryMode=>"edges");|
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : vertexConnectivity G                                                |
|                                                                         |
|o2 = 1                                                                   |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note minimalVertexCuts: minimalVertexCuts, -- finds the minimal vertex
    cuts of a graph
  * *note vertexCuts: vertexCuts, -- lists all the vertex cuts of a graph
  * *note edgeConnectivity: edgeConnectivity, -- computes the edge connectivity
    of a graph

Ways to use vertexConnectivity:
===============================

  * "vertexConnectivity(Graph)"

For the programmer
==================

