vertexCovers -- returns a list of the minimal vertex covers of a graph
**********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        V = vertexCovers G
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * V, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the list of minimal vertex covers
        of graph G

Description
===========

A vertex cover of G is a set of vertexSet which intersects with every edge of
G. In other words, L is a vertex cover of a graph if and only if their does not
exist an edge {u,v} such that both u and v are not in L.

+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : G = graph({{1,2},{1,3},{1,4},{2,3}},EntryMode=>"edges");|
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : vertexCovers G                                          |
|                                                             |
|o2 = {{1, 2}, {1, 3}, {2, 3, 4}}                             |
|                                                             |
|o2 : List                                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note vertexCoverNumber: vertexCoverNumber, -- returns the vertex cover
    number of a graph
  * *note coverIdeal: coverIdeal, -- Returns the vertex cover ideal of a graph

Ways to use vertexCovers:
=========================

  * "vertexCovers(Graph)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note vertexCovers: vertexCovers, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

