vertexCuts -- lists all the vertex cuts of a graph
**************************************************

  * Usage: 
        C = vertexCuts G
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * C, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the list of vertex cuts of a
        graph

Description
===========

A vertex cut is a set of vertices that, when removed from a graph, make the
graph have more than one component.  The complete graph has no vertex cuts, so
the method returns an empty list.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : G = cycleGraph 5;                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : vertexCuts G                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = {{0, 2}, {0, 3}, {1, 3}, {0, 1, 3}, {0, 2, 3}, {1, 4}, {2, 4}, {0, 2,   |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     4}, {1, 2, 4}, {1, 3, 4}}                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note minimalVertexCuts: minimalVertexCuts, -- finds the minimal vertex
    cuts of a graph
  * *note vertexConnectivity: vertexConnectivity, -- computes the vertex
    connectivity of a graph
  * *note edgeCuts: edgeCuts, -- returns the edge cuts of a graph

Ways to use vertexCuts:
=======================

  * "vertexCuts(Graph)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note vertexCuts: vertexCuts, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

