vertexMultiplication
********************

  * Usage: 
        H = vertexMultiplication (G, v, u)
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 
      * u, a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, u is the new vertex to be added
      * v, a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, v is the vertex whose neighbors
        become the vertices that u connects to.
  * Outputs:
      * H, a *note graph: Graph,, 

Description
===========

Multiplying the vertex of a graph adds one vertex to the original graph. It
also adds several edges, namely, if we are multiplying a vertex v and calling
the new vertex u, {u,W} is an edge if and only if {v,w} is an edge.

+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : G = completeGraph 5              |
|                                      |
|o1 = Graph{0 => {1, 2, 3, 4}}         |
|           1 => {0, 2, 3, 4}          |
|           2 => {0, 1, 3, 4}          |
|           3 => {0, 1, 2, 4}          |
|           4 => {0, 1, 2, 3}          |
|                                      |
|o1 : Graph                            |
+--------------------------------------+
|i2 : H = vertexMultiplication(G, 0, 6)|
|                                      |
|o2 = Graph{0 => {1, 2, 3, 4}   }      |
|           1 => {0, 2, 3, 4, 6}       |
|           2 => {0, 1, 3, 4, 6}       |
|           3 => {0, 1, 2, 4, 6}       |
|           4 => {0, 1, 2, 3, 6}       |
|           6 => {1, 2, 3, 4}          |
|                                      |
|o2 : Graph                            |
+--------------------------------------+

Ways to use vertexMultiplication:
=================================

  * "vertexMultiplication(Graph,Thing,Thing)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note vertexMultiplication: vertexMultiplication, is a *note method
function: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

